{"id": "tech-3", "headline": "FCC tells California to stop enforcing phone rules against AT&T", "source": "Ars Technica", "url": "https://arstechnica.com/tech-policy/2026/11/fcc-orders-california-to-stop-enforcing-phone-service-rules-against-att/", "published": "2026-11-20", "url_verified": true, "pages": ["The Federal Communications Commission ordered California on Friday to stop enforcing its Carrier of Last Resort rules against AT&T, Ars Technica reports. The rules require AT&T to offer phone service to anyone in its territory. AT&T wants to stop basic service to new customers and end service for 184,000 residential and 15,000 business customers on June 1, 2027, replacing it with wireless home phone service. A federal judge rejected AT&T's attempt to override the state rules in July. FCC Chairman Brendan Carr said the rules were \"designed for a bygone era\". California says wireless replacements must still meet its standards. The state could sue the FCC.", "AT&T has won relief in 20 of the 21 states where it has wireline service. Source: Ars Technica"], "qr": {"n": 41, "rows": ["11111110110101001111111110000111101111111", "10000010011111000010011101100100001000001", "10111010101000000011100001101000001011101", "10111010110110101011001011100100001011101", "10111010100111100001100011111101001011101", "10000010011111000111011011100001001000001", "11111110101010101010101010101010101111111", "00000000011100000110000100000110100000000", "11110010111100101111011010111101010011101", "10110000001010001001011110101111101111001", "11010111010110101100000100001010011110110", "01000100101001101000000101111011010000010", "01010110111110010010101011010101100001110", "00010100000110001101000010111001011001111", "11110010100100111101010011001111101011011", "01001000010100001010110000001010101111010", "00100010110011010010110011000011110010010", "11000101101110010100111100010100110101010", "10110011101001111100110000111100010110000", "11010001001111110001101010001101001101110", "